title: '[EPMB] Add configurable reward source and slash destination to signed phase'
doc:
- audience: [Runtime Dev]
  description: |-
    Adds two new associated types to `pallet-election-provider-multi-block::signed::Config`:

    - `type RewardSource: Get<Option<Self::AccountId>>`: when set to `Some(pot_account)`, rewards
      are paid via a balance transfer from the given pot account rather than being minted directly
      into the winner's account. If the transfer fails (e.g. insufficient pot funds), the reward is
      silently skipped. When `None` (default), the previous mint behaviour is preserved.

    - `type Slash: OnUnbalanced<Credit<Self::AccountId, Self::Currency>>`: handler for slashed
      deposits. When `()` (default), slashed funds are burned (same as previous behaviour). Runtimes
      with DAP-based issuance (e.g. Polkadot / Westend Asset Hub) should set `type Slash = Dap` to
      redirect slashed funds to the DAP buffer instead of destroying them.

    Both changes are motivated by the DAP (Delegated Authorship Pool) issuance model on Asset Hub,
    where the total issuance must remain reconcilable against the fixed DAP emission curve. The
    previous `mint_into` and `burn_held` calls silently inflated or deflated `TotalIssuance` outside
    that model, making the hard cap invariant unenforceable.

    The `Currency` bound gains `fungible::BalancedHold` (re-exported as `BalancedHold` from
    `frame_support::traits::tokens::fungible`) to enable the `slash` method used for the new
    slash routing.

    **Migration**: existing runtime configurations must add `type Slash = ();` and
    `type RewardSource = frame_support::traits::ConstNone;` (or an equivalent `Get<Option<…>>`
    returning `None`) to their `signed::Config` impl to preserve the current behaviour.

crates:
- name: pallet-election-provider-multi-block
  bump: major
